<title>UK: Black Sea, Baltic oil exports up 420k bpd in week.</title>
<headline>Black Sea, Baltic oil exports up 420k bpd in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total oil exports, including crude oil and refined products, from Baltic and Black Sea terminals rose nearly 420,000 barrels per day (bpd) the first week of January, analysts Petro-Consultants said.</p>
<p>The Geneva-based Petro-Consultants, using tanker tracking data, said total crude oil exports from the former Soviet Union using the Black Sea and Baltic terminals averaged 1.18 million bpd, up nearly 380,000 bpd from the week earlier and up more than 200,000 bpd from the same week in 1996.</p>
<p>But gas oil shipments from the terminals, including those from Romania and Bulgaria, were 290,575 bpd, down a sharp 71,457 bpd from the last week of December.</p>
<p>Total fuel oil shipments averaged 311,119 bpd, up 54,900 bpd on the week and a hefty 248,241 bpd up on a year ago.</p>
